        "text": "It was a walk-in clinic, but I went there twice for nothing. The first time was because it was too early in my pregnancy for the prenatal test. I had tried to contact them by phone to find out the requirements for my blood test, but without success. The second time was because they were out of vials for the blood draws. It seems to me that vials and syringes are pretty much the bare minimum for a blood collection center. I finally went to the Hawkesbury clinic. I wasn't able to take advantage of the promotion on their website because apparently it required a special request from the doctor. My regular request didn't work. I had to follow up with them twice to get my results. They finally sent them, but to the wrong clinic. I received them almost a month and a week later, just as I was approaching my 17th week and my bump was starting to show. Luckily, the results were negative.",
